> If you want to help others, it can never be wrong.

A compelling story about morality driven by an incredible performance by Kamal Haasan. Throughout the film, we as the audience go back and forth between supporting Velu's actions or deeming them too far. It's hard not to sympathize with him, however we see the consequences of his actions. Revenge is a double edged sword. The more he loses, the more he seeks vengeance and the more he seeks vengeance, the more he loses, culminating in a phenomenal scene with Velu and his daughter. "Who are you to decide what's right or wrong? Are you god?"

A fantastic portrayal of the cycle of hatred.

Great soundtrack as well. "Thenpaandi Cheemayile" is a classic.
